# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC and is served as bookdup.io — and its working tree doubles
# as the agent workspace, so internal files sit right next to deployable pages.
#
# Brief 146 hardened this after a `git add -A --dry-run` showed 170 internal
# files would have been staged, including a Twilio recovery code and a 140-row
# lead list. Nothing internal has ever actually been committed — this is
# preventive. It stays preventive only if this file stays committed.
#
# Rule of thumb: this repo tracks WEBSITE CONTENT ONLY. If it is not an .html
# page, CNAME, .nojekyll or README.md, it almost certainly does not belong here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Credentials and secrets — never commit
.env
*.env
*.env.*
!.env.example

# Mandatory Credential Injection Protocol temp files
.tmp-cred-*
*.tmp-cred
*token*.txt
*pat*.txt
*secret*.txt
*.keys

# Credential-adjacent filenames. twilio_recovery.txt matched none of the patterns
# above and would have been committed — hence the broader wording here.
*recovery*
*credential*

# Client and lead data — PII plus commercially sensitive contact lists
*.csv
memory/
**/data/*.json
data/

# Internal agent workspace docs. Every .md in this tree is internal except the
# repo README, so the rule is deny-by-default rather than a list that has to be
# updated each time a new doc appears — there are already ~60.
*.md
!README.md

# Internal agent state, briefs and tooling
.openclaw/
briefs/
skills/
agent-bridge/

# Sibling projects that live inside this working tree but are versioned
# separately. Git treats these as embedded repos, so `git add -A` would stage a
# bare gitlink rather than their contents — but ignoring them removes the
# ambiguity and the "adding embedded git repository" warning entirely.
barber-receptionist/
bookdup-legal/

# Stale duplicate of the site. Brief 145 removed the one tracked page here after
# it was found publicly served with pricing that was never real. The remaining
# files are uncommitted local drafts; keep them out so the orphan cannot return.
bookdup-website/

# Backups — working files, never part of the deployed site
*.bak
*.bak-*
*_backup_*

# Node modules
node_modules/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.log

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
